---
layout: layout.njk
title: Table
description: Homepage direction — the table.
section: Directions
permalink: /table/index.html
bodyClass: page-table
---

<div class="deck">
  <header class="deck-intro">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Direction C · not locked</p>
      <h1>The docket on the table.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Information is the service. The past board is populated. Upcoming is empty by design — and it sits to the side.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/docket/">Full docket</a>
      <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/offer-book/">Offer book</a>
      <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/brief/">Brief</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="deck-sittings" aria-labelledby="sat-heading">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="sat-heading">Sat · <span class="tabular">{{ pastSittings.length }}</span></h2>
      <p class="legend">
        <span class="chip chip-owned">Owned</span>
        <span class="chip chip-co-hosted">Co-hosted</span>
        <span class="chip chip-listed">Listed</span>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="docket-lines">
      {% for sitting in pastSittings %}
      <li class="line line--{{ sitting.relation }}">
        <a href="/docket/{{ sitting.slug }}/">
          <span class="meta">{{ sitting.startsAt | nyDay }} · {{ sitting.relation | relationLabel }}</span>
          <strong>{{ sitting.title }}</strong>
        </a>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <aside class="deck-rail">
    {% set emptyTitle = "No sitting is on the docket yet." %}
    {% set emptyBody = "Upcoming always resolves. An empty upcoming list is a designed state." %}
    {% include "empty.njk" %}
  </aside>
</div>
